  "published_at": "2026-08-12T15:00:41.654Z",
  "id": 203987063212842,
  "uuid": "cf8d6a6d-9735-490a-9d94-58c75ca7524c",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "22e1f2f0-aa22-c0e7-563d-27f5e4f4661e",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "4da8a88a-a8a1-ae6f-0844-234855d8e314",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The event was a collaborative effort between SPIE, the student-led simulation society, and the CIME team. They conducted three engaging sessions at the TDF Museum, where participants enjoyed a hands-on, holistic learning experience. Every session of the workshop featured four interactive stations:",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Electrocution Station: Participants learned how to handle electric currents and shocks safely.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "CPR Station: Children were taught basic CPR skills with the guidance of a CPR professional.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Burn Station: Participants learned how to manage burns effectively.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Bleeding Station: Children were taught techniques to stop bleeding instantly.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The workshop served as a qualitative research tool for the education team at CIME to study parental perceptions of community-based simulations for teaching children life-saving skills. The workshop successfully combined education with excitement, leaving a lasting impact on the participants.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
